        /* The element is producing sound. Nothing else moves 'loading' on:
           LOAD and PLAY are intents, and only the element knows when they
           took. Without this a track sat at 'loading' for as long as it
           played, so TICK ignored it (no position, no play count until the
           very end) and the first press of the transport meant "play" and
           did nothing audible. It is also how a resume from outside the app,
           a media key or a headset, reaches a paused state. */
